voicing lock, and complete      Billing plan: reopen, release, and complete      Invoicing document: set print lock and remove print lock      Billing request: cancel, reject, send for checking, and release    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 54 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Welcome Message Translation\nDescription: The welcome message will appear in the user's preferred language based on their language settings. This ensures that Joule is presented in a language you are comfortable with, rather than the default English.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 55 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule for Microsoft 365 Copilot\nDescription: By integrating Joule and Microsoft 365 Copilot, you can leverage the Joule capabilities from within Microsoft 365 Copilot Business Chat. For more information, see Using Joule with Microsoft 365 Copilot.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-30\nValid as Of: 2025-05-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 56 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Support for Documents in TXT File Format\nDescription: The document grounding capability now supports documents in TXT file format.  See Set Up Document Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-23\nValid as Of: 2025-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 57 ---\nComponent: Joule,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UX Improvements to Joule in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: Scenario flows and texts have been optimized for Joule interactions.  Joule in the cockpit now supports multiple attributes when selecting entities. For example, you can select a subaccount by entering the subaccount display name, subaccount ID, and/or subdomain name. Joule validates the name you enter and provides suggestions should it not recognize your entry.  Entities and attributes:  Cloud Foundry Space: ID name, space name  Global Account: subdomain, display name  User: email address  Role Collection: name  Region: region (technical name), display name  Subaccount: ID, display name, subdomain  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 58 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Multi Conversation\nDescription: The Multi Conversation feature allows you to execute long running queries or asynchronous queries, or start conversations with Joule on multiple topics in parallel. This allows you to start multiple conversations in parallel on different topics. Conversation Threads also allows you to delete selected threads, rename threads, and access conversation history. With this feature, the idle timeout for a conversation thread expiry has been increased from 15 minutes to 8 hours.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-24\nValid as Of: 2025-04-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 59 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: User Feedback\nDescription: Each Joule response now features Thumbs ups and Thumbs down icons that can be used to record user feedback. Users can click the thumbs up icon to indicate that they have liked the response. Alternatively, if a user finds a response unsatisfactory, clicking the thumbs down button will open a list of options from which the most appropriate reason for the\",698\n458,\"--- Record 1881 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription: You can now configure additional HTTP request headers if you have BTP destinations of OData or REST API types. These headers are useful when working with the Data flow functions. To learn more, see Configuring Additional HTTP Request Headers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-25\nValid as Of: 2024-11-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1882 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Option for Creating Actions Project Using BAPIs and RFCs\nDescription: We're introducing the new capability to create Actions project using BAPIs and RFCs. This feature empowers you to integrate seamlessly with SAP systems, leveraging BAPIs and RFCs for robust and dynamic interactions. By using this functionality, you can explore and integrate SAP systems more effectively, thereby enhancing your project's capabilities and overall efficiency. As a result, you can consume these Actions within your business processes and applications, driving greater productivity and value.  See Using RFCs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-23\nValid as Of: 2024-11-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1883 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Support to Documents in Static HTML File Format\nDescription: The document grounding capability now supports documents in static HTML file format.  See Set Up Document Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-27\nValid as Of: 2024-11-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1884 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Provisioning - Search for Tenant by Customer Name and ID\nDescription: You can now search for tenants using Customer Name and Customer ID.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-11-20\nVersion: 3.4\n\n--- Record 1885 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Trust List Entry Per Credential Type\nDescription: You can now restrict the trust of a trusted issuer by credential type.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-11-20\nVersion: 3.4\n\n--- Record 1886 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.27.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Metrics: You can export lifecycle statistics for your Deployment, StatefulSet, DaemonSet, and Job resources with selectors in the runtime input of a MetricPipeline (#1521).      Metrics: Cluster-level metrics (without namespace attribute) are no longer dropped if the runtime input defines a namespace filter (#1549).      Logs: Improved health reporting for the AgentHealthy status of a LogPipeline (#1545).      Logs: Increased memory limit to prevent unnecessary restarts of Fluent Bit Pods (#1586).      Improved printColumns for Telemetry CRD (#1560)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-06\nValid as Of: 2024-11-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1887 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-19\nValid as Of: 2024-11-19\nVersion: 26995\n\n--- Record 1888 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry) - write transformation\nDescription: Conditions for user and group entities in the default write transformation are enhanced to support the landscape property along with the group prefix.  See SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-19\nValid as Of: 2024-11-19\nVersion: 26995\n\n--- Record 1889 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry) - write transformation\nDescription: Conditions for user and group entities in the default write transformation are enhanced to support the landscape property along with the group prefix. Combining the landscape of the multi-environment subaccount with Cloud Foundry environment with the group prefix ensures that only entities from that particular landscape matching the specified group prefix will be provisioned to the corresponding SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry) target system.  For more information, see SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-19\nValid as Of: 2024-11-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1890 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\n\",464\n83,\"--- Record 91 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: You no longer have to create the NavigationService destination in your subaccount while setting up Joule integration, as it is created automatically via the Joule booster.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-09\nValid as Of: 2024-12-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 92 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Now Available in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition.\nDescription: Joule is now available in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition for the following use cases:      Navigation to a selection of apps 